---
// COMPLIANCE COMPONENT — read before editing.
//
// Legend Story Studios' Terms of Use for Game and Studio Assets and IP grant
// third-party applications like this one a written permission, on conditions.
// Two of those conditions live in this file:
//
//   1. The disclaimer must appear verbatim, in the footer, on every page. The
//      text is not written here — it comes from the single exported constant
//      required by docs/COMPLIANCE.md, so there is exactly one place a typo
//      can live. Render it as one text node; never split it across elements
//      and never reflow it.
//
//   2. No Flesh and Blood or Legend Story Studios logos or set symbols may
//      appear anywhere on the site — product set logos count as FAB logos.
//      Nothing in this footer is a mark, and nothing here should become one.
//
// Presentation now comes from the token layer, as Phase 1 said it would. The
// *text* is still not Phase 1's to change, and is not changed here.
import { LSS_DISCLAIMER } from "../lib/compliance";

/*
 * THE METHOD CLAIM LIVES HERE NOW, ONCE, RATHER THAN ON THE PAGES THAT FELT
 * LIKE SAYING IT.
 *
 * The front door carried "N cards, last confirmed …, nothing here is
 * summarised, paraphrased or generated" under the card row, and `/search`
 * carries a longer version of the same sentence under its results. Both are
 * true and neither belonged where it was: a claim about how the whole corpus is
 * made is not a property of one screen, and repeating it per page makes it read
 * as reassurance rather than as a fact about the data.
 *
 * `docs/PLAN.md` asks that a stale Optfall look stale. Saying this beside the
 * licence terms does that on all 7,238 pages, which is where somebody checking
 * our claims is already looking.
 *
 * THE COUNTS ARE DELIBERATELY NOT HERE, and the reason is a measured one. This
 * footer renders on every page, so anything it imports becomes a dependency of
 * every page — pulling the corpus in for two numbers took the build from about
 * 10 seconds to about 30. The counts are already where they are earned: the
 * front door's "Browse all N cards" link, and `/search`, which serves the data
 * and states its upstream commit beside it.
 */
---

<footer class="compliance">
  <p class="disclaimer">{LSS_DISCLAIMER}</p>
  <p class="licence">
    Optfall's own code is MIT-licensed. Published datasets are openly licensed
    only over the structural work this project owns — rule identifiers, the
    legality timeline, diffs and annotations. <a href="/data-terms">Data terms</a>.
  </p>
  <!--
    Inline elements stay on the same source line as the text around them: the
    build drops the whitespace at a line break falling immediately before an
    inline tag.
  -->
  <p class="provenance">Nothing here is summarised, paraphrased or generated.</p>
</footer>

<style>
  /* A hairline rule, not a box. `docs/DESIGN.md`: density is held together by
     tight vertical rhythm and hairline rules rather than cards and shadows. */
  .compliance {
    margin-block-start: var(--of-space-loosest);
    padding-block-start: var(--of-space-looser);
    border-block-start: var(--of-ornament-rule-width) solid var(--of-color-rule);
    /* `ink.muted`, NOT `ink.faint`, and the difference is a compliance one.
       This footer carries the LSS disclaimer — the one piece of text the
       licence requires to be present — at `type.size.micro`, which is small
       body copy and therefore needs 4.5:1, not the 3:1 large-text threshold.
       `ink.faint` measures 3.86:1 dark and 3.63:1 light against the ground and
       would have put the required notice below AA on every page. `ink.muted`
       measures 8.09:1 and 6.33:1, and is the token `tokens.test.ts` asserts in
       its BODY_TEXT set at 4.5:1. */
    color: var(--of-color-ink-muted);
    font-size: var(--of-type-size-micro);
    line-height: var(--of-type-leading-loose);
  }

  /* Muted by token rather than by `opacity`: opacity dims text against
     whatever happens to sit behind it, which makes the contrast unknowable and
     therefore unassertable. */
  .compliance p {
    margin-block: 0 var(--of-space-base);
  }

  .compliance p:last-child {
    margin-block-end: 0;
  }
</style>
